Subject: [PATCH] test(control): pin what a pixel drag selects on cascadia

The rule a user feels is the composition of two quantisations -
std::round at the press site, std::floor plus a direction fudge at the drag
anchor - so it cannot be read off either one. This drives PointerPressed and
PointerMoved in pixels against a real ControlCore and reads the selection back,
sweeping both endpoints across whole cells.

What it found, and now pins:

  dragging right: [ floor(press.x / w) , round(drag.x / w) )
  dragging left:  [ round(drag.x / w)  , floor(press.x / w) + 1 )

The cell the drag started on is always selected whole, and where inside it the
press landed makes no difference - the first drag movement re-anchors and
throws the press site's rounding away. That is stated as its own test, because
that rounding looks load-bearing and is not; taking it at face value is what
sent ghostty's anchor a character late.

